Neil W. McCabe and Steve Bannon Discuss U.S. Support for Strikes Against Iran

Bannon: Saying there aren’t going to be any attacks until after the midterms is just saying, ‘We know how much people hate this, and we’re going to wait until after the vote takes place.’ That’s not quieting things down. I think that's throwing gasoline on the fire. We’re either going to go back to kinetic war, or we’re going to work with the Russians and use Scott Bessent’s economic-warfare program. I don’t think there’s any appetite whatsoever to go back to kinetic war, except in Israel and among AIPAC and that crowd. I was on one of the original combatants—a destroyer sent to the North Arabian Sea and the Persian Gulf in 1979–80. My kid brother was over there in 1986–87, and my daughter was in Iraq in 2010–11. The Bannons are a typical American family that served their country. We hate all of it; we want to come home. We should come home. We shouldn’t be back in Qatar. 
@ReporterMcCabe

JOHN SOLOMON: The Pentagon quietly issued guidance going back to what the law says. If you are an American citizen who has never set foot in the United States, you cannot vote.

This won’t affect military voters. It affects the children of expats sitting in Europe and Asia who have never been engaged in American society, and Democrats have long organized every one of those voters.

@jsolomonReports
